My goal was to build an ESPHome based drop in replacement controller.

I built 2 controllers. A dummy controller with no interface (all controlled via ESPHome) and a Touch Screen based on a 7" ESP32 touch screen.

The analog control is handled by a pair of X9C 10k digital potentiometers which seemed to be the simplest way to go about this.

I ended up using 3 switches (and hid the pump switch from the UI) Didn't bother with a thermostat card because that isn't how a swamp cooler really is designed to work.

So,
My 3 switches are
1 - Ducted AC (Main control)
2 - Cooling Mode (pump control)
3 - Pump (Hidden from the UI, Does stuff based on switches 1 and 2)



# ESPHome Examples

# Completely Optional but added a DHT11 Temp Humidity Sensor
sensor:
  - platform: dht
    pin: GPIO14
    temperature:
      name: "House Temperature"
      id: AC_Therm
    humidity:
      name: "House Humidity"
    update_interval: 60s



# Digital Potentiometers
#I X9c for the Pump. I could probably have done this with a divider but the X9C is cheap enough
output:
  - platform: x9c
    id: Pump_gpio
    cs_pin: GPIO5
    ud_pin: GPIO0
    inc_pin: GPIO4
    inverted: True
    ### EVAP PUMP Values
#    min_power: 1
    max_power: 0.50

# Fan Speed control. Logic inverted here so pulling the X9C High will turn the fan off
  - platform: x9c
    id: Fan_gpio
    cs_pin: GPIO15
    ud_pin: GPIO12
    inc_pin: GPIO13
    inverted: True
    ### Evap AC FAN Values
    # I had to tweak these to best match the voltages my original controller was providing. Min and Max voltage were suficient.
    min_power: 0.20
    max_power: 0.79

# Fan control 
fan:
  - platform: speed
    name: "Ducted Air Conditioning"
    output: Fan_gpio
    speed_count: 10
    id: fan_Ducted
    on_turn_on: 
      then:
        - if:
            condition:
              - lambda: 'return id(cooling_mode).state;'
            then:
              - switch.turn_on: Pump_out

    on_turn_off: 
      then:
        - switch.turn_off: Pump_out

switch:
# The actual pump switch hidden from the UI.
  - platform: output
    output: Pump_gpio
    id: Pump_out

# Cooling mode switch, Doesn't actually do anything if the fan is off.
  - platform: template
    id: cooling_mode
    name: "Cooling"
    optimistic: True
    on_turn_off: 
      then:
        - switch.turn_off: Pump_out
    on_turn_on: 
      then:
        - if:
            condition:
              - lambda: 'return id(fan_Ducted).state;'
            then:
              - switch.turn_on: Pump_out

# Example thermostat config, I wasn't a huge fan of this because a swamp cooler can't really control the temp like an evap can
climate:
  - platform: thermostat
    id: swamp_cooler
    name: "Swamp Cooler"
    min_idle_time: 
      seconds: 30
    min_cooling_off_time: 
      seconds: 30
    min_cooling_run_time: 
      minutes: 5
    min_fanning_off_time: 
      seconds: 30
    min_fanning_run_time: 
      minutes: 5
    sensor: AC_Therm  # Temperature sensor
    cool_action:
      - switch.turn_on: Pump_out
      - fan.turn_on: fan_Ducted
    fan_only_action:
      - switch.turn_off: Pump_out  # Ensure pump is off in fan-only mode
      - fan.turn_on: fan_Ducted
    idle_action:
      - switch.turn_off: Pump_out
      - fan.turn_off: fan_Ducted
